#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# key_take

#% text
# `key_take(a, [k, ...])` gives the entries of the keys given that the association `a` has, in that order.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A list of rules is read as an association; a list of associations gives the list of results.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
key_take(assoc(a -> 1, b -> 2, c -> 3), [c, a])
#% output
#= assoc(c -> 3, a -> 1)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A list of associations:

#% cell
key_take([assoc(a -> 1, b -> 2), assoc(a -> 3)], a)
#% output
#= [assoc(a -> 1), assoc(a -> 3)]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `key_drop`, `lookup`, `keys`
